---
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
export const prerender = true;

const updated = 'September 28, 2026';
---

<TextPage
  title="Privacy *Policy*"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} (${SITE.domain}) collects, uses and protects your personal information.`}
>
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {updated}</p>

  <p>
    Welcome to {SITE.name} ("we", "us", "our"), available at <a href="/">{SITE.domain}</a>. We care about your privacy
    and collect as little personal information as possible. This Privacy Policy explains what we collect, why we
    collect it, how we protect it, and the choices you have.
  </p>
  <p>By using our website, you agree to the practices described in this policy.</p>

  <h2 id="summary">The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can read every pattern on this site <strong>without creating an account</strong> or giving us any personal information.</li>
    <li>We only collect personal information that <strong>you choose to send us</strong>: your email for the newsletter, or your details when you contact us.</li>
    <li>We <strong>do not sell, rent or trade</strong> your personal information.</li>
    <li>We do not use advertising cookies or tracking pixels.</li>
    <li>You can ask us to see, change or delete your information at any time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="what-we-collect">1. Information we collect</h2>

  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Newsletter sign-up:</strong> your email address.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> your name, your email address and the message you write.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Please don't include sensitive information (such as health or financial details) in messages you send us.</p>

  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical data:</strong> like almost every website, our hosting provider automatically processes basic
      technical information when you visit, such as your IP address, browser type, device type, the pages you request
      and the date and time of your visit. This is used to deliver the website, keep it secure and prevent abuse.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Theme preference:</strong> if you switch between light and dark mode, your choice is saved in your own
      browser's local storage so the site remembers it. This stays on your device and is never sent to us.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="how-we-use">2. How we use your information</h2>
  <p>We use your information only to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>send you the newsletter you signed up for, with new patterns and site updates;</li>
    <li>read and reply to your messages and questions;</li>
    <li>run, maintain, secure and improve the website;</li>
    <li>detect and prevent spam, fraud and abuse;</li>
    <li>comply with legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="legal-basis">3. Legal basis (for visitors in the EU, UK and similar regions)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consent</strong> – when you subscribe to our newsletter. You can withdraw consent at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> – to answer your messages and to keep the website secure and working.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> – when the law requires us to keep or share certain information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="cookies">4. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>
    We do not use advertising or analytics cookies. We use your browser's local storage only to remember your light
    or dark mode preference, as described above. Our hosting and security provider (Cloudflare) may set strictly
    necessary cookies to protect the website from attacks and bots.
  </p>
  <p>If we ever add analytics or advertising, we will update this policy and ask for your consent where the law requires it.</p>

  <h2 id="sharing">5. How we share your information</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information. We only share it with trusted service providers who help us run the website:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> – hosts our website and stores our database (including newsletter emails and
      contact messages), and protects the site from attacks.
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Fonts</strong> – we load our fonts from Google, so your browser connects to Google's servers
      and shares your IP address with them.
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also share information if required by law, to respond to valid legal requests, or to protect the rights,
    safety and property of {SITE.name}, our visitors or others.
  </p>

  <h2 id="transfers">6. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Our service providers may process data in countries other than yours, including the United States. When this
    happens, we rely on the safeguards these providers offer, such as standard contractual clauses, to protect your
    information.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">7. How long we keep your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Newsletter emails:</strong> until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete them.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact messages:</strong> up to 24 months, so we can follow up on your question, then deleted.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical logs:</strong> kept by our hosting provider for a short period, according to its own policy.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="security">8. How we protect your information</h2>
  <p>
    The website is served over a secure, encrypted connection (HTTPS), and access to our database is restricted and
    protected. No method of storing or sending data over the internet is 100% secure, but we take reasonable steps to
    protect your information.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-rights">9. Your rights and choices</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the personal information we hold about you;</li>
    <li>correct information that is wrong or incomplete;</li>
    <li>delete your information;</li>
    <li>object to or restrict how we use it;</li>
    <li>receive a copy of your information in a portable format;</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent at any time;</li>
    <li>complain to your local data protection authority.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Unsubscribing:</strong> you can unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time by using the unsubscribe link
    in our emails or by <a href="/contact">contacting us</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>California residents:</strong> we do not sell or "share" personal information for targeted advertising
    as those terms are defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA).
  </p>
  <p>To make any request, please <a href="/contact">contact us</a>. We will reply within 30 days.</p>

  <h2 id="children">10. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our website is intended for a general audience and is not directed at children under 13 (or under 16 in the
    EU). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has sent us personal
    information, please <a href="/contact">contact us</a> and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="links">11. Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Our patterns may link to other websites, such as yarn shops or tutorials. We are not responsible for the privacy
    practices of those websites, so please read their privacy policies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">12. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will change the "Last updated" date at the
    top of this page. If the changes are important, we will let newsletter subscribers know.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">13. Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or your personal information, please send us a message
    through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
  <p>See also our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>.</p>
</TextPage>
